Shadow GL_POLYGON_OFFSET_LINE client-side and apply a projection-row
depth bias around polygon-mode line draws.

GLES has only GL_POLYGON_OFFSET_FILL, and that enable offsets triangles,
not GL_LINES. gl4es already lowers glPolygonMode(GL_LINE) to
gles_glDrawArrays(GL_LINES), so the desktop LINE enable was a silent
GL_INVALID_ENUM and glPolygonOffset(0.1, -1000) never pulled outlines
off their faces. gl-repl's vertex-outline pass is built on that enable.

This patch:

- shadows GL_POLYGON_OFFSET_LINE in enable.c (GO, not proxy_GO: do not
  forward the enum to GLES) and answers glIsEnabled from the shadow;
- saves/restores the LINE enable on GL_ENABLE_BIT and GL_POLYGON_BIT;
- mirrors glPolygonOffset / glPolygonOffsetx factor and units (x is
  16.16) and restores both on GL_POLYGON_BIT via gl4es_glPolygonOffset
  so glPushAttrib(GL_ALL_ATTRIB_BITS) cannot leak (0.1, -1000) into
  the next scene;
- caches GL_ALIASED_LINE_WIDTH_RANGE (hardext.maxlinewidth) and
  GL_DEPTH_BITS (default 16, clamp [8, 32]) once when a GL context
  exists. The Emscripten notest path has no context yet, so it keeps
  the safe defaults (max linewidth 1, depth bits 16) instead of
  probing through an unset WebGL context;
- lands a shared MV/P save/poke/restore helper that dirties mvp,
  inv_mv, and normal on both poke and restore;
- applies P_row2 += d * P_row3 around polygon-mode line draws, with
  d = 2 * units * 2^{-depth_bits} / (Far - Near), |d| <= 1. Cached
  object-space line_arrays are never written. GLES FILL-around-lines
  is a no-op, so this is the width-1 mechanism.

Independently testable at width 1: glIsEnabled(GL_POLYGON_OFFSET_LINE)
round-trips, glEnable no longer raises GL_INVALID_ENUM, PushAttrib
restores enable and factor/units, and a width-1 outline-over-face
screenshot of polygon-mode / GLUT solids stops speckling. Genuine
GL_LINE_LOOP (including the tessellation overlay) is out of scope --
native _LINE never applied to line primitives.

Applied by scripts/web-deps.sh after gl4es-point-size-batch.patch
(needs the polygon-line DrawArrays path). Must also sit after
gl4es-pushattrib-gaps.patch (same stack.c polygon block).
